#X obj 652 11 metro.random;
#X obj 230 93 cnv 1 535 393 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 98 Random distribution: uniform;
#X text 240 123 The object behaves like a regular metronome \, but
the interval between successive bangs is chosen randomly and uniformly
within the range set by @min and @max. The range can be changed at
any time through the second and third inlets or via a list of the form
min max. The generator can be made deterministic by setting @seed to
a non-zero value.;
#X text 240 239 Use case in algorithmic composition: stochastic pulse.
A composer can use [metro.random] to drive a granular or percussive
texture where each event occurs at an unpredictable moment within a
chosen window. By slowly sweeping @min and @max from wide to narrow
values \, the texture gradually transforms from a sparse \, scattered
cloud of events into a dense rhythmic stream.;
#X text 240 355 Use case in an installation: unpredictable ambient
triggers. In a sound installation the object can trigger short sounds
at irregular intervals so that the space never seems to repeat itself.
The range of intervals may be linked to sensor data \, for example
the number of people in the room \, so that the density of events grows
naturally with the activity of the visitors.;
